\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Is k-WL equivalence with k supplied as part of the input EXPTIME-complete under deterministic polynomial-time many-one reductions, both for general finite uncolored graphs and when both graphs have maximum degree three?

\subsection{Short English statement}
Is k-WL equivalence with k supplied as part of the input EXPTIME-complete under deterministic polynomial-time many-one reductions, both for general finite uncolored graphs and when both graphs have maximum degree three?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Variable-dimension-Weisfeiler-Leman-equivalence-on-general-and-subcubic-graphs-September-25-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

